# Raw source dumps: regenerable in about a minute with tools/fetch_sources.py,
# and they change every week when citation counts are refreshed.
data/raw/

# LaTeX build products inside digested-paper directories
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Downloaded paper scans. These are the published articles themselves: not ours
# to redistribute, and this repository is public. Each paper directory's
# notes.md records the source URL, so a copy can always be re-fetched.
# What IS tracked is our own work on them: <name>-original.tex (transcription),
# <name>-expanded.tex/.pdf (the digestion), ledger.md, notes.md.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*/*.pdf
![0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*/*-original.pdf
![0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*/*-expanded.pdf
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*/*-source.tar.gz

# Readings: theses and expository work that a paper's digestion draws on. These are
# tracked, because the site links to them as local files (`readings` in papers.json,
# `local: true`) and a clone with the file missing is a dead link. Unlike the scans
# above, these are included with their author's knowledge.
![0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*/*-reading.pdf
